<title>USA: Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.95		    $0.89</p>
<p> Net			121,000		  108,000</p>
<p> Net revs		 854,000		  833,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 120,400		  114,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>	  SIX MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.11		    $1.68</p>
<p> Net			265,000		  212,000</p>
<p> Net revs	     1,779,000		1,654,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 119,400		  115,900</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTES: Q2 principal transactions revenues fell 18 percent to $326 million from $398 million.</p>
<p>Q2 investment banking revenues rose 23 percent $274 million from $223 million.</p>
<p>Q2 commissions revenues fell three percent to $91 million $94 million.</p>
<p>Q2 compensation and benefits expenses rose three percent to $433 million from $422 million.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
